- Oh. feel free.

290
00:20:42.197 --> 00:20:44.751
Good. First. you're a slob.

291
00:20:44.949 --> 00:20:46.924
You dress like a bum.

292
00:20:47.061 --> 00:20:49.396
Second. you're unmotivated.

293
00:20:49.974 --> 00:20:53.270
You have no self-esteem.
no thought about the future.

294
00:20:53.655 --> 00:20:57.681
You're inconsiderate. You're insensitive.
You're insincere.

295
00:20:58.712 --> 00:21:02.869
I'm having the same caterer for your shower
that we had at our Christmas party last year.

296
00:21:03.032 --> 00:21:05.105
That'd be great! They're wonderful!

297
00:21:05.241 --> 00:21:09.911
If I were you. I'd worry less about the shower
and more about Rick's bachelor party.

298
00:21:10.138 --> 00:21:13.521
Why...? Why would I want
to do that? I trust Rick.

299
00:21:13.691 --> 00:21:17.620
Oh. of course you do.
And I trusted my ex. Kevin. too.

300
00:21:18.587 --> 00:21:21.141
Cousin. I can only speak to you
from experience.

301
00:21:21.307 --> 00:21:23.730
But what do you think happens
at bachelor parties?

302
00:21:24.124 --> 00:21:26.743
Think they drink tea and play Scrabble?

303
00:21:26.940 --> 00:21:28.947
Llene. I trust Rick. He promised...

304
00:21:29.053 --> 00:21:32.217
Debbie. please! Don't be naive. Men are pigs.

305
00:21:33.342 --> 00:21:36.822
Girls. why don't we go inside
and have some lunch?

306
00:21:38.014 --> 00:21:40.731
Boys! Come on inside and have lunch!

307
00:21:41.054 --> 00:21:42.996
In a second.

308
00:21:44.607 --> 00:21:47.738
And you're irresponsible. A show-off.

309
00:21:48.032 --> 00:21:50.453
You're vulgar. You're inappropriate.

310
00:21:50.912 --> 00:21:54.077
You're unrefined. You're obnoxious.

311
00:21:54.592 --> 00:21:59.514
Well. Mr Thompson. that's really quite a list.
And you're right. You're absolutely right.

312
00:21:59.649 --> 00:22:02.878
And I think. if I really apply myself.

313
00:22:03.011 --> 00:22:07.353
I could be a totally changed person
by the time we finish lunch.

314
00:22:18.852 --> 00:22:21.088
Rick. we don't have a dog.

315
00:22:21.668 --> 00:22:25.826
Oh. too bad. That's a waste of some good fat.
Are you going to eat your potato. darling?

316
00:22:25.990 --> 00:22:28.324
- You want this?
- You betcha.

317
00:22:28.485 --> 00:22:31.104
Yeah. me and Debbie are
gonna have kids right away.

318
00:22:31.334 --> 00:22:34.683
I'd like to adopt this 17-year-old
Korean girl I've had my eye on.

319
00:22:34.855 --> 00:22:38.499
I figure why beat around the bush.
but. I mean. this pup is fertile.

320
00:22:38.695 --> 00:22:41.729
and I know I'm perfectly capable.
so you don't have to worry.

321
00:22:41.895 --> 00:22:44.995
You'll have some American grandkids
in no time at all.

322
00:22:45.385 --> 00:22:48.997
I tell ya. Mrs T. this is really some spread.
This is pretty good chow.

323
00:22:49.225 --> 00:22:51.811
Usually I just have ajam sandwich for lunch.

324
00:22:52.074 --> 00:22:56.646
Do you know what ajam sandwich is? You
take two pieces of bread. jam 'em together...

325
00:23:02.315 --> 00:23:05.731
- Hello. everybody! Am I late?
- Not at all. We're just finishing lunch.

326
00:23:05.931 --> 00:23:07.840
- How are you. Cole?
- Fine. just fine.

327
00:23:07.948 --> 00:23:10.436
Ilene! You're looking very well.

328
00:23:12.268 --> 00:23:14.408
- Mrs Thompson...
- Cole...

329
00:23:14.573 --> 00:23:16.515
Always a pleasure.

330
00:23:20.878 --> 00:23:22.788
Debbie...

331
00:23:22.894 --> 00:23:24.269
And. uh...

332
00:23:24.847 --> 00:23:27.181
Bond. James Bond.

333
00:23:28.687 --> 00:23:31.404
So. Cole. how's your game coming along?

334
00:23:31.952 --> 00:23:34.440
- Better and better. sir.
- Good.

335
00:23:34.640 --> 00:23:36.614
I'll take you on.

336
00:23:36.945 --> 00:23:39.945
We tried some doubles this morning
but it didn't work out.

337
00:23:41.168 --> 00:23:43.341
Mother. what is Cole doing here?

338
00:23:44.466 --> 00:23:47.019
Well. you know your father
enjoys his company.

339
00:23:47.250 --> 00:23:51.211
Oh. he must. if he took time off
from his Hitler Youth rally.

340
00:23:54.802 --> 00:23:57.137
- Good shot!
- Thank you. sir.

341
00:23:58.228 --> 00:24:04.110
Cole. I know you're as unhappy as I am
about Debbie's marriage to Rick.

342
00:24:04.500 --> 00:24:06.442
Yes. I am. sir.

343
00:24:08.630 --> 00:24:12.208
- Son. I don't want you to give up on her.
- I have tried to change her mind.

344
00:24:12.758 --> 00:24:17.297
It's not her mind you have to change.
It's Mr Shit For Brains in there.

345
00:24:17.942 --> 00:24:22.482
- Yeah. but how can I do that?
- If it were up to me. I'd reason with him first.

346
00:24:22.711 --> 00:24:26.159
And if that failed.
I'd try more persuasive action.

347
00:24:29.049 --> 00:24:32.278
More... persuasive action?

348
00:24:35.449 --> 00:24:39.127
Good... Keep me informed.

349
00:24:42.106 --> 00:24:43.601
Goodbye. darling.

350
00:24:43.835 --> 00:24:47.097
Goodbye. Mom.
Thanks for everything. It was great.

351
00:24:47.227 --> 00:24:51.603
- Nice seeing you again. Rick.
- You too. Mrs T. Let's do this every day.

352
00:24:51.772 --> 00:24:55.001
- How about tomorrow? I'll bring weenies.
- Well. I have. uh... club.

353
00:24:55.164 --> 00:24:58.461
- What time's it over?
- Uh. Rick. Let's talk.

354
00:24:59.709 --> 00:25:02.360
Honey. the boys have something to discuss.

355
00:25:02.558 --> 00:25:05.275
Let's leave 'em alone for a minute. huh?

356
00:25:06.302 --> 00:25:09.205
If this is about the facts of life.
I got it covered.

357
00:25:09.311 --> 00:25:12.029
- Rick. I want Debbie.
- You do. huh?

358
00:25:12.256 --> 00:25:14.645
Yes. I do.
You dump her and I'll give you cash.

359
00:25:14.815 --> 00:25:17.816
Well. what's Debbie's
Blue Book value right now?

360
00:25:17.952 --> 00:25:20.287
- $5.000.
- No.

361
00:25:20.416 --> 00:25:22.140
- 7500?
- Not interested.

362
00:25:22.336 --> 00:25:24.410
All right. all right. all right.

363
00:25:24.577 --> 00:25:28.407
10.000 plus a GE toaster oven.

364
00:25:28.513 --> 00:25:31.034
a Litton microwave. a Cuisinart...

365
00:25:31.202 --> 00:25:33.145
Cole. read my lips now.

366
00:25:33.251 --> 00:25:35.617
I am marrying Debbie.

367
00:25:36.483 --> 00:25:37.912
Michelin tyres. brand-new.

368
00:25:38.115 --> 00:25:40.504
A set of Sears' best metric tools.

369
00:25:42.788 --> 00:25:44.064
What's going on?

370
00:25:44.197 --> 00:25:48.475
This big lug is in love and he's got
a lot of major appliances laying around.

371
00:25:48.773 --> 00:25:53.629
Debbie. Cole is just trying to save you
from making a mistake. A big mistake.

372
00:25:54.054 --> 00:25:55.548
Oh. Daddy...

373
00:25:55.718 --> 00:25:58.402
Hey. thanks. Dad. Listen. we gotta go.

374
00:26:00.070 --> 00:26:02.721
Debbie! He's gonna hurt you.

375
00:26:03.335 --> 00:26:06.303
He'll never be true to you the way I would.

376
00:26:08.008 --> 00:26:11.303
We'll keep that in mind.
Cole Whittier. ladies and gentlemen!

377
00:26:11.592 --> 00:26:16.132
A funny. funny guy as well as being
a wonderfully talented human being.

378
00:26:16.297 --> 00:26:18.567
Take care. babe. We love ya.

379
00:26:18.954 --> 00:26:21.508
Hey. Rick! You and I. we're not through yet.

380
00:26:40.845 --> 00:26:42.187
Hey...

381
00:26:42.637 --> 00:26:44.011
Hey...

382
00:26:44.141 --> 00:26:45.221
What?

383
00:26:45.390 --> 00:26:47.333
I can't sleep.

384
00:26:48.526 --> 00:26:50.861
I got something for that.

385
00:26:57.936 --> 00:27:01.067
Will you stop fooling around? I need to talk.

386
00:27:01.201 --> 00:27:02.859
What's the matter?

387
00:27:03.088 --> 00:27:05.510
I don't know. I just feel scared.

388
00:27:06.320 --> 00:27:09.354
Oh. baby... What about?

389
00:27:10.386 --> 00:27:12.328
Hmm?

390
00:27:15.250 --> 00:27:17.640
The wedding. My parents.

391
00:27:17.842 --> 00:27:20.014
Your parents. Our friends.

392
00:27:20.179 --> 00:27:21.423
My job.

393
00:27:21.555 --> 00:27:22.897
The future.

394
00:27:23.059 --> 00:27:24.488
Our relationship.

395
00:27:24.660 --> 00:27:27.181
The caterers. My gown.

396
00:27:27.636 --> 00:27:29.579
Your tuxedo.

397
00:27:30.388 --> 00:27:32.942
The honeymoon. Our apartment.

398
00:27:33.109 --> 00:27:34.538
My shower.

399
00:27:34.773 --> 00:27:36.715
Your bachelor party.

400
00:27:38.325 --> 00:27:42.221
Well. how about the Middle East?
You all right with that?

401
00:27:42.487 --> 00:27:44.789
Honey. everything is gonna be all right.

402
00:27:44.983 --> 00:27:48.660
Before or after I have
my nervous breakdown?

403
00:27:55.609 --> 00:27:57.780
You are so tense.

404
00:27:58.297 --> 00:28:00.272
Come on.

405
00:28:02.329 --> 00:28:04.304
That feels so good.

406
00:28:04.762 --> 00:28:06.867
That's a coincidence. It's supposed to.

407
00:28:07.034 --> 00:28:10.581
Close your eyes. Drift off to sleep again. OK?

408
00:28:11.323 --> 00:28:14.836
Ltjust so happens... I'm a great guy

409
00:28:15.451 --> 00:28:20.819
and. very soon.
you're gonna be Mrs Great Guy. all right?

410
00:29:02.754 --> 00:29:06.170
Well. there you go. ma'am.
End of the line. Last stop.

411
00:29:06.372 --> 00:29:10.595
I have a great idea. Why don't I just
pal around with you guys for a while?

412
00:29:10.787 --> 00:29:16.156
No. no. no. We have some manly things we
have to do. and this is no place for a woman.

413
00:29:16.357 --> 00:29:19.586
- Are you sure you don't want me to go?
- How about "no"?

414
00:29:19.718 --> 00:29:21.693
I don't wanna go!

415
00:29:25.094 --> 00:29:27.331
Remember.
you promised me no screwing around.

416
00:29:27.495 --> 00:29:30.562
- I won't! I swear on my mother's grave.
- Your mother's not dead.

417
00:29:30.728 --> 00:29:33.062
Well. if I go back on my word. I'll kill her.

418
00:29:34.664 --> 00:29:36.093
Have a good time.

419
00:29:38.024 --> 00:29:41.156
Don't have a great time.
You catch my drift. Mr Traditional Guy?

420
00:29:41.321 --> 00:29:43.231
Hmm. yeah. I understand.

421
00:29:43.337 --> 00:29:46.436
And you have a fun shower. Use soap.

422
00:29:50.955 --> 00:29:52.449
I love you.

423
00:29:52.651 --> 00:29:54.593
And I love you.

424
00:29:57.804 --> 00:30:00.138
Come on. Rick! Party!

425
00:30:09.133 --> 00:30:13.641
Presidents have stayed in this suite.
It's gorgeous!

426
00:30:15.086 --> 00:30:17.061
What presidents?

427
00:30:18.670 --> 00:30:22.250
- What's wrong?
- Nothing. Nothing. Let's get crazy.

428
00:30:22.640 --> 00:30:24.582
Yeah!

429
00:30:26.351 --> 00:30:31.274
- When do the girls show up?
- Gary is taking care of that right now.

430
00:30:36.082 --> 00:30:39.148
All right. I think I've got
just what you're looking for.

431
00:30:39.314 --> 00:30:40.395
Great.

432
00:30:40.531 --> 00:30:42.091
Margot! Darleen!

433
00:30:43.123 --> 00:30:45.424
These are twins of pleasure.

434
00:30:47.059 --> 00:30:49.033
Wow! Twins!

435
00:30:49.364 --> 00:30:50.095
Great!

436
00:30:50.291 --> 00:30:52.975
They're gonna be just fine. Just fine.

437
00:30:54.581 --> 00:30:55.759
Hi. ladies.

438
00:30:55.893 --> 00:31:00.978
Maybe after the orgy tonight we can get
together. have a cup of coffee or somethin'?

439
00:31:01.557 --> 00:31:04.492
<i>Thanks. man. We'll see you girls later. Ciao!</i>

440
00:31:25.017 --> 00:31:26.675
Hi!

441
00:31:28.313 --> 00:31:29.110
Hi.

442
00:31:29.305 --> 00:31:31.794
Say. I must have just missed my friend.

443
00:31:31.994 --> 00:31:34.613
He hired some of your girls
for a bachelor party?

444
00:31:34.810 --> 00:31:39.089
Yeah. Parkview Hotel. room 1002.
What about it?

445
00:31:39.548 --> 00:31:42.996
Yeah. right. well. um...
here's the new address.

446
00:31:43.164 --> 00:31:47.223
